.TH KISA-CCE-COLLECT 8 "2026-09-03" "KISA CCE Linux Scanner" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
kisa-cce-collect \- collect live runtime evidence for an offline KISA CCE scan
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kisa-cce-collect
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kisa-cce-collect
captures a bounded snapshot of the live Linux host identity, systemd units,
listeners, mounts, firewall state, and time synchronization state.
Directory permissions restrict access to the owner. Supply the directory to
.BR kisa-cce-scan (8)
with
.BR \-\-evidence-bundle .
.PP
Run the collector as root on the live system immediately before taking the
corresponding offline filesystem snapshot.
It does not create an archive, probe remote services, refresh package metadata,
or collect authentication secrets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
Create or use an empty absolute directory for the evidence bundle.
The directory must be root-owned, must have mode 0700, and must not be a
symbolic link.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the evidence schema version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Every terminal line begins with a dmesg-style uptime prefix with six
fractional digits, including help, version, errors, warnings, and the completed
bundle path. The collector falls back to safe process time or zero when
.I /proc/uptime
is unavailable. On success, the collector prints:
.PP
.EX
[    12.345678] kisa-cce-collect: evidence_bundle=/absolute/path
.EE
.PP
The directory contains a manifest with a strict schema, SHA-256 checksums,
host identity, normalized service, listener, and time-synchronization tables,
raw mount information, and firewall state. The collector writes evidence schema
version 2.
All files use mode 0600 and all directories use mode 0700.
.PP
The normalized time table supports systemd-timesyncd, Chrony, ntpd-rs, and
NTPsec. When ntpd-rs is installed, the collector parses
.B "ntp-ctl status"
and records the source identity and stratum, then discards the raw command
output. Resolved addresses for the same pool share one record. More than one
distinct source identity makes schema version 2 collection partial. Service
activation is recorded separately as an
.I ntpd-rs.service
fact.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The collector finalized the bundle.
Optional runtime sources may still be marked partial or unavailable in the
manifest.
.TP
.B 2
Invocation, identity collection, output security, or finalization failed.
.TP
.B 130
The process received SIGINT.
.TP
.B 143
The process received SIGTERM.
.SH SECURITY
The bundle contains sensitive infrastructure metadata.
Protect it as security assessment data during storage and transfer.
SHA-256 checksums detect changes after capture. They do not, by themselves,
authenticate the collector or transport.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kisa-cce-scan (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ss (8),
.BR proc_pid_mountinfo (5)
